{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T01:33:27Z","created_by_operation":"op_422ea83d26e94216951e659e75377eec","id":"pg_1e029e2b69765514bda5dde50377261a","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/anthropics-claude-agent-sdk-python-claude-md-37a52c9fb3f0-dde50377261a.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_a9b4f523a1755b86a2b3eaf9070ed87a"],"title":"anthropics/claude-agent-sdk-python/CLAUDE.md @ 37a52c9fb3f0","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:33:27Z","updated_by_operation":"op_422ea83d26e94216951e659e75377eec"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_118091d0972494b5c04814d489939d17f6989c51fad8f37e8f954d8a295e121a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Hooks are Python functions invoked by the Claude Code application at points of the agent loop, e.g. a PreToolUse matcher that can deny a Bash command by pattern."},{"claim_ids":["clm_1c8491ad259e7576f1bf9254da4d52c365c0fca6a0db3280f2afd4da0d790fc8"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The SDK exposes an async query() function that returns an AsyncIterator of response messages, with a ClaudeAgentOptions configuration object."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3b7d3cacea18debf4844ef00b9854e8ca935727d38ec65de8b177acbe53996b6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"ClaudeSDKClient supports bidirectional interactive conversations and, unlike query(), additionally enables custom tools and hooks defined as Python functions."},{"claim_ids":["clm_958187aab2fe766b5073b185e6ebc858030cc2c6561a3e3a835019bd968ec40f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: releases are published to PyPI via a manually triggered GitHub Actions workflow that builds platform wheels bundling a chosen CLI version and opens a version-update PR."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a6518366c72ae5b8cab5e8d77e0455ffc14b1ebc71e5d494217f72123045566e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"ClaudeAgentOptions supports both in-process SDK MCP servers and external stdio subprocess MCP servers in the same mcp_servers mapping."},{"claim_ids":["clm_abd472a33ebb7736903065ed582edfc3647f4885d6236cfc9f315e0fd8fd196d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Custom tools are implemented as in-process SDK MCP servers running inside the host Python application, avoiding subprocess management and IPC overhead of external MCP servers."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d782b5c6f20e3e4455dd08bad704723fd93a34c5ed75758911a8f4fc4dea5f01"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: contributors run ./scripts/initial-setup.sh to install a pre-push hook that runs lint checks matching CI, skippable with git push --no-verify."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d79ad534167853fc40bbece7c4a8b5d987c082116ff7fda1b47269c280ce9bb3"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The SDK defines typed message and content-block types (AssistantMessage, UserMessage, SystemMessage, ResultMessage, TextBlock, ToolUseBlock, ToolResultBlock) and an error hierarchy including CLINotFoundError, ProcessError, and ResultError."},{"claim_ids":["clm_e6eececddeb3ae7da43a035c66369f2a70de17356585c16bf1a93c9903bf5222"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The package requires Python 3.10+ and bundles the Claude Code CLI by default; a system CLI or custom cli_path can be specified instead."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f0e282972d9c2b11a6434118b7bb67ccb065473210cc15d0fbb046af5df633db"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"By default Claude has the full Claude Code toolset; allowed_tools is an auto-approval allowlist that does not remove tools, while disallowed_tools blocks tools, and permission_mode and can_use_tool handle unlisted tools."}],"claim_ids":["clm_118091d0972494b5c04814d489939d17f6989c51fad8f37e8f954d8a295e121a","clm_1c8491ad259e7576f1bf9254da4d52c365c0fca6a0db3280f2afd4da0d790fc8","clm_3b7d3cacea18debf4844ef00b9854e8ca935727d38ec65de8b177acbe53996b6","clm_958187aab2fe766b5073b185e6ebc858030cc2c6561a3e3a835019bd968ec40f","clm_a6518366c72ae5b8cab5e8d77e0455ffc14b1ebc71e5d494217f72123045566e","clm_abd472a33ebb7736903065ed582edfc3647f4885d6236cfc9f315e0fd8fd196d","clm_d782b5c6f20e3e4455dd08bad704723fd93a34c5ed75758911a8f4fc4dea5f01","clm_d79ad534167853fc40bbece7c4a8b5d987c082116ff7fda1b47269c280ce9bb3","clm_e6eececddeb3ae7da43a035c66369f2a70de17356585c16bf1a93c9903bf5222","clm_f0e282972d9c2b11a6434118b7bb67ccb065473210cc15d0fbb046af5df633db"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T01:33:27Z","created_by_operation":"op_422ea83d26e94216951e659e75377eec","id":"pg_6ddf16125d705bd0a445d95db92e597c","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/anthropics-claude-agent-sdk-python-readme-md-37a52c9fb3f0-d95db92e597c.md","re